4. Simplified the component structure
5. Wrapped the UserListTable with our mock data injection HOC
6. Added error feedback UI in case of rendering issues

This approach:
- Doesn't rely on global window modifications
- Provides better error handling
- Keeps the mock data contained within the component
- Uses React patterns (HOC) to inject the mock data
- Maintains the necessary provider structure

The component should now either render properly with the mock data or show a helpful error message if something goes wrong. This should help us better understand what's happening if there are still issues.

